# NTSD-M12-ANDROID-DECODE-UPLOAD-BACKPRESSURE-001

## Implementation-01 current supplement

Direct human approval of Driver/App shutdown scope supersedes the historical proposed-only statements below. Exact stage1 cancellation / stage2 actual image drain / stage5 staging cleanup and async normal App shutdown follow shutdown-review-01/REPORT.md, with no stage reorder. Current code is IN_PROGRESS and uncompiled. Manager admission/drain helpers were first written; remaining registration APIs and wiring are pending. No runtime result claimed.

Correction: active reservations are bounded by admitted bytes and finite declared jobs, NOT by CPU4+upload1+one waiter. More than six small completed CPU jobs can wait for upload. Every launched task must drain even after a fault; cancellation cannot zero counters. Immutable descriptor owner is one invocation; no global image cache. Diagnostics are fixture-owned, cold-only and default null, no tick hook. Metrics retain numbers only; actual pixel arrays are counted by reference identity and retained staging ownership is reported separately.

Minimum sequence: original Editor compile; descriptor and reservation finite tests; actual blocked image worker shutdown pending/resume/recreate guard; unchanged head-callback shutdown tests; shared ON/OFF pixel/catalog and public caller fixture; only if all pass one fixed same-input ABBA. First runtime hard failure stops later runtime/cost groups. Compile repairs allowed with new preimages. A retains old float lifetime, B releases it after plans. No full content load, Player or device test.

Subagent correction: 01a12a3f-e571-7d80-b199-50fe7504934b was assigned BMPLoader only, then stopped before any write. Its final report confirms zero changed/new files and source SHA d94a25e9d70cb658366fc5539f345d0dfadb21e5354588bf2d39aca9ee6cdaaf equals backup. Main thread owns all remaining work; no further delegation. Operation baseline and revision preimages are in implementation-01.

